                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Cost of Bariatric Surgery</h2>

                <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">The cost of bariatric surgery in Delhi typically ranges from INR 2,50,000 to INR 5,00,000 depending on the surgical technique used, such as gastric bypass or sleeve gastrectomy, and the patient's choice of hospital ward. This includes diagnostic tests, surgeon fees, anesthesia, operating theater usage, and the hospital stay. Laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy costs between INR 2,50,000 and INR 3,50,000, while Roux-en-Y gastric bypass ranges from INR 3,50,000 to INR 5,00,000. Undergoing this treatment at SCOD Clinic with the <a href="https://scodclinic.com/services/bariatric-surgery" class="text-scod hover:text-blue-700 font-semibold">Best Bariatric Surgeon in Delhi</a> and utilizing insurance coverage drastically reduces your personal out-of-pocket expenses.</p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Steps to Get Insurance Approval</h2>

                <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">To get bariatric surgery insurance approval, you must obtain a detailed recommendation from a specialist, gather your medical reports documenting failed non-surgical weight loss attempts, and submit a pre-authorization form to the third-party administrator (TPA). The typical approval process involves these key steps:</p>
                <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-gray-600 mb-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong>Consultation:</strong> Consult <a href="https://scodclinic.com/about" class="text-scod hover:text-blue-700 font-semibold">Dr. Arush Sabharwal</a> at SCOD Clinic to evaluate your eligibility.</li>
                    <li><strong>Diagnostic Evaluation:</strong> Undergo evaluations like cardiac clearances and sleep studies to document co-morbidities.</li>
                    <li><strong>Document Assembly:</strong> Compile your prescription, surgeon recommendation, and history of weight loss attempts.</li>
                    <li><strong>Pre-Authorization Submission:</strong> The hospital billing desk will submit these with a pre-authorization form to your TPA (such as Paramount Health Services TPA Pvt Ltd or Medi Assist India TPA Pvt Ltd) at least 7 to 10 days prior to your surgery for cashless approval.</li>
                </ol>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Reasons Why Insurance Claims Get Rejected</h2>

                <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">Bariatric surgery insurance claims get rejected primarily when the insurance provider classifies the procedure as a cosmetic treatment, when the patient fails to disclose pre-existing illnesses like chronic high blood pressure, or when critical medical documents are missing. Common reasons for rejection include:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 mb-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong>Cosmetic Classification:</strong> The claim is rejected if the insurer suspects the procedure is cosmetic (such as when the patient's BMI is below 35 without co-morbidities).</li>
                    <li><strong>Waiting Period Restrictions:</strong> Rejections occur if the surgery is performed during the policy's initial pre-existing disease waiting period.</li>
                    <li><strong>Non-Disclosure of Pre-Existing Illnesses:</strong> Failing to declare pre-existing conditions like hypertension or diabetes when purchasing the policy will lead to claim denial.</li>
                    <li><strong>Incomplete Documentation:</strong> Submitting incomplete surgeon notes, missing diagnostic reports, or lack of proof of failed non-surgical weight loss attempts can stall or reject the claim.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">Consulting the <a href="https://scodclinic.com/services/bariatric-surgery" class="text-scod hover:text-blue-700 font-semibold">Best Bariatric Surgeon in Delhi</a> at SCOD Clinic helps prevent these rejections by ensuring all documentation is thoroughly prepared for TPAs like Vidal Health TPA Private Limited.</p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Tips to Choose the Right Insurance Plan</h2>

                <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">You can choose the right insurance plan for bariatric surgery by comparing the waiting periods, selecting a policy with a high sum insured of at least INR 5,00,000, and checking for exclusions or co-payment requirements. Keep these tips in mind when selecting a plan:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 mb-6 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong>Shorter Waiting Periods:</strong> Prioritize plans with shorter waiting periods for pre-existing conditions, preferably 2 years instead of 4 years.</li>
                    <li><strong>Adequate Sum Insured:</strong> Opt for a high sum insured of at least INR 5,00,000, since weight loss surgeries typically cost between INR 2,50,000 and INR 5,00,000.</li>
                    <li><strong>No Co-Payment Clauses:</strong> Look for policies with no co-payment requirements to avoid paying a percentage of the claim out of pocket.</li>
                    <li><strong>Comprehensive Coverage:</strong> Verify that the policy covers pre- and post-hospitalization costs, including diagnostic tests, nutritional consultations, and follow-up medications.</li>
                    <li><strong>Network Hospitals:</strong> Check that top-tier facilities like SCOD Clinic are in the insurer's network for cashless treatment.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Conclusion</h2>

                <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">In conclusion, bariatric surgery insurance coverage is a vital financial tool that makes life-saving weight loss surgery accessible and affordable for patients struggling with severe obesity. Since the IRDAI mandates coverage for medically necessary bariatric surgery, patients no longer have to bear the entire financial burden of this treatment. By choosing a plan with a shorter waiting period, disclosing pre-existing conditions, and keeping detailed medical reports, you can successfully claim your surgical expenses. Consulting a specialist like <a href="https://scodclinic.com/about" class="text-scod hover:text-blue-700 font-semibold">Dr. Arush Sabharwal</a> at SCOD Clinic provides both the clinical expertise and the documentation support needed for a smooth claim process.</p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

                <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">Here are the answers to the most common questions regarding bariatric surgery insurance coverage in India, helping you navigate the process of claim approval.</p>

